cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MedAgent Workbench in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "MedAgent Workbench: a local-first, model-agnostic medical research agent workbench"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "LyZheFeng"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LyZheFeng/medagent-workbench"
license: MIT
version: 0.8.0
date-released: 2026-11-15
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - medical research
  - clinical evidence
  - diagnostic accuracy
  - reproducibility
  - local-first
  - desktop application
abstract: >-
  A medical fork of Open Science Desktop for research and teaching: clinical
  evidence synthesis (PICO, Oxford CEBM, GRADE), diagnostic-accuracy statistics
  with confidence intervals, CARE-aligned case reports, literature review and
  citation checking, each with provenance for the artifacts it produces. Not a
  medical device; it does not provide diagnostic or treatment advice.
# The upstream project this fork derives from. Cite it too when the work that is
# actually being relied on is the shared base (shell, runtime, provenance,
# gateway, computer use) rather than the medical layer.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Open Science Desktop: a local-first, model-agnostic AI research workbench"
    authors:
      - name: "The Open Science Desktop Contributors"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/ai4s-research/open-science"
    url: "https://openedscience.com"
    version: 0.7.1
    license: MIT
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23755472
    date-released: 2026-10-29